{
	title: '/mem: host memory',
	spec: '/mem shows the host process memory on one screen, in a code fence, numbers humanized (B, KB, MB, GB): RSS; JS heap used of capacity and object count (bun:jsc heapStats); the machine free of total memory; and the holders Hal knows about: each open session with its loaded history record count and bytes (history.state.cache, which readSync keeps for open sessions), the page-mark files pages keeps, and the web bundle size (not built until first requested). Read-only; it never triggers GC unless called as /mem gc, which runs Bun.gc(true) and shows the report before and after. Anything else after /mem is a usage error. Code: src/host/commands/mem.ts; listed in common/commands/list.ts as a debug command a model may use.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'There is no in-memory blob cache (attachments live on disk), so "blob caches" became the history cache and page marks, the two caches that exist. Run /mem gc twice to see heap settle: the first collection itself allocates.'
	],
	needs: ['x0']
}
